\[I_{x}(10,6) = Q(F|12,20) = .10\text{ where }x = \frac{20}{20 + 12F}\]

From Table 26.9 the upper 10 percent point of \(F\) with 12 and 20 degrees of freedom is _F_=1.89. Hence

\[x = \frac{20}{20 + 12(1.89)} = .469\]

The correct value to 4D is _x_=.4683.

